## Fill null with value

To replace null values with the next value that follows them, use the Polars expression `backward_fill` as shown below:

::: {#4b7b58c4 .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(df
 .with_columns(pl.col('Number').backward_fill())
 )
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (5, 2)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>Company</th><th>Number</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>i64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Meta&quot;</td><td>1001</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Facebook&quot;</td><td>1001</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Google&quot;</td><td>1020</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;OpenAI&quot;</td><td>2304</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Oracle&quot;</td><td>1022</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


Now the values in *Number* are filled. The opposite of this method is `forward_fill`.

